WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:04.040
Just being at your side,

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:16.160
Gentles my hearts to the point of disbelief

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:25.570
I thought I heard the sound of your footsteps behind me,

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:35.720
I turned my head repeatedly, wishing you would appear...

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:41.740
...and then there you were

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:50.990
The beginning of a new love

00:00:51.310 --> 00:01:05.870
Is unknowingly, the beginning of our invisible love story

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:15.360
Hence, I shall never leave your side

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:24.540
I pledge to love you and only you

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:40.570
Tetsu...

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:46.280
Tetsu!

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:53.320
Fuyumi...

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:57.260
It hurts...

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:02.640
I can't... take it... anymore!

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.440
Kill me...

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:09.570
Kill me, Fuyumi!

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:12.630
It hurts!

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.650
I can't! I can't do that!

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:21.490
Sorry.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:24.690
Sorry, Fuyumi.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:29.900
You dummy, Tetsu.

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:32.070
Why are you crying?

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:39.200
Here, touch my breast.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:41.630
Fuyumi...

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:49.110
Fuyumi, I'm so scared!

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:52.680
I'm...

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.160
I'm done for...

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:01.150
I can't take the pain!

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:05.660
Come on, there's nothing to cry about!

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:08.560
See, doesn't that feel good?

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:11.170
Love me, Tetsu!

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:13.500
Until the very end!

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:18.480
I love you... Fuyumi!

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:25.520
Rest now.

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:29.560
You've done your job.

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:33.430
Now rest in peace.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:38.900
But Tetsu, why didn't you call my name...

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:41.100
even once?

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:43.390
Stupid Tetsu!

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:50.250
<i>I was alone on this planet,</i> <i>guilty of so many crimes,</i>

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:57.440
<i>but still he was kind to me,</i> <i>treating me as a girl.</i>

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:02.780
<i>He died calling out a name,</i> <i>his wife's name,</i>

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:05.720
<i>the one he loved.</i>

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:12.030
Tetsu, I'll deliver your letter to her.

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:23.600
<i>This is all I can bear to</i> <i>write about this man.</i>

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:47.200
Haven't you had enough playing war games?

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:51.170
I guess it's time for me to get to work.

00:04:55.450 --> 00:05:00.140
<i>Shuji, today I wiped out</i> <i>another city.</i>

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:04.800
<i>It was just another big,</i> <i>meaningless battle.</i>

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:08.090
<i>A day when many people died.</i>

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:12.660
<i>Shuji, pretty soon now...</i>

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.250
<i>In just a bit...</i>

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:15.550
Akemi!

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:19.530
<i>I'll be home again...</i>

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:22.190
<i>in my hometown.</i>

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:31.440
<i>To my dearest classmate, Shuji...</i>

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:36.310
<i>is there peace in our town?</i>

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:43.470
"And Then..."

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.990
<i>The school was closed down.</i>

00:05:50.170 --> 00:05:51.880
<i>Earthquake victims,</i>

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:56.140
<i>and refugees from the mainland</i> <i>that had been sheltered there</i>

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:58.470
<i>were sent away, and tomorrow,</i>

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.840
<i>it will become headquarters</i> <i>for the retreating army.</i>

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:07.080
<i>Today was the last day for this class.</i> <i>More than half were gone anyway.</i>

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:12.820
<i>Who could have imagined this back</i> <i>when I started dating Chise?</i>

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:16.090
<i>And had we known,</i>

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:20.520
<i>would we have done anything different?</i>

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:25.560
So Chise asked you out, huh?

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:30.230
Don't try to deny it. Yukari told me.

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:32.440
So what?!

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:35.140
Does Akemi know about this?

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:37.370
It was Akemi's idea.

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:42.010
So, are you going to say yes?

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:44.150
You should!

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:46.050
It might be your only chance!

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:47.680
Don't you start too!

00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:49.120
Shuji, take a look!

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:51.290
Hey, Yukari!

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:53.020
Take!

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:56.930
<i>Would we...</i>

00:06:57.530 --> 00:06:59.900
<i>have broken up like that, anyway?</i>

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:03.000
Shuji!

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:07.780
<i>Tonight, the sophomores</i>

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.110
<i>are having a farewell party.</i>

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:15.180
<i>The Cultural Festival is cancelled,</i>

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:16.980
<i>but at least,</i>

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:19.960
<i>they'll have something to remember.</i>

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:22.760
<i>That's the way it should be.</i>

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:26.050
<i>After all, we haven't lived</i> <i>all that long.</i>

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:36.870
Shuji, it's my dad.

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:45.480
Are you sure it's OK, all this stuff?

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:48.110
They can't pay you for it.

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:52.850
That's alright. I want them to enjoy their festival.

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:53.550
"Festival"?

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:57.550
I like festivals.

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:01.390
We need them in times like these.

00:08:04.070 --> 00:08:07.500
And this way the military won't get this stuff.

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:10.940
They should've been here when we needed them,

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:13.110
not straggling in now.

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:17.880
I bought this wine when Akemi was born.

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:23.320
I meant to drink it with her when she got old enough.

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:30.260
We would've talked about the man in her life and things like that.

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:34.360
Would you drink it with her?

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:36.690
I, uh...

00:08:39.070 --> 00:08:43.300
She loved to run. Now she's beaten me to the finish line.

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:46.530
Thanks, huh?

00:08:47.180 --> 00:08:51.480
While I was running around looking for a doctor,

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:54.450
even though I knew she had no chance,

00:08:55.230 --> 00:08:58.250
you were with her at the end.

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:01.920
Shuji, thank you!

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:10.730
Shuji!

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:12.360
What is it?

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:15.130
The army's here.

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:16.640
What do they want?

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:20.270
They're taking over the school now instead of tomorrow.

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:22.370
They say we have to cancel the party!

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:26.380
You know this is an emergency, don't you?

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:31.150
Yes, but we've been working all day getting ready for this!

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:33.180
I don't give a damn!

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:37.620
We're fighting to protect people like you!

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:40.220
Many of our comrades are dead!

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:44.130
Please wait till tomorrow!

00:09:44.530 --> 00:09:45.690
Who're you?

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:49.900
I'm a senior. I want them to have their party.

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:52.540
What? Don't you get it?! Now--

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:53.440
Look here!

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:58.910
<i>I know a lot of you have</i> <i>been killed.</i>

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:01.380
<i>And I know how you must feel.</i>

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:06.820
<i>But what have any of you</i> <i>done to help us?</i>

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:10.190
<i>What did you do for Akemi?</i>

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:15.060
<i>Our friends have died in front of us</i> <i>and we couldn't do anything!</i>

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:17.700
Well? Speak up!

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:23.850
We may be kids, but we're not stupid.

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:27.400
I beg you! Please!

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:29.440
Please!

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:33.810
Please let us have our party!

00:10:33.950 --> 00:10:34.610
Please!

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:39.250
<i>Damn it, I feel so stupid!</i> <i>Is this all I can say?!</i>

00:10:40.190 --> 00:10:42.250
<i>But we know.</i>

00:10:42.730 --> 00:10:44.990
<i>This country is finished.</i>

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:46.270
- Please! - Please!

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.760
<i>We know why the army</i>

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:53.670
<i>is here in Hokkaido.</i>

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:55.840
<i>Why Atsushi hasn't returned...</i>

00:10:57.140 --> 00:10:59.470
<i>why there are so many earthquakes...</i>

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:02.410
<i>and why everyone...</i>

00:11:03.380 --> 00:11:05.610
<i>wants this party so badly.</i>

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:11.780
<i>What we fear most,</i>

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:15.820
<i>more than war,</i> <i>or even death itself...</i>

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:19.130
<i>is dying without having</i> <i>our silly party.</i>

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:22.460
<i>Dying with feelings of regret...</i>

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:25.490
<i>that we never did anything.</i>

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:35.810
Akemi...

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:40.510
don't tell me how un-cool I was.

00:11:44.790 --> 00:11:48.220
I know already.

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:55.730
Listen to your little sister and them having fun.

00:11:57.800 --> 00:12:02.900
It's the last day of school. We better get back to class.

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:07.970
Atsushi'll be mad if we leave him out.

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:20.710
<i>Shuji, wait for me, OK?</i>

00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:26.990
<i>There's one more thing</i> <i>I have to do before I see you.</i>

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:32.300
<i>It'll be quick, so wait for me.</i>

00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:40.000
<i>Shuji, It's OK.</i>

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:43.800
<i>I'm a bit stronger now.</i>

00:12:44.350 --> 00:12:45.180
<i>Wait for me.</i>

00:12:49.590 --> 00:12:53.920
<i>But if I come flying in,</i> <i>you'll get mad at me again.</i>

00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:55.910
<i>So I'll walk.</i>

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:15.470
Don't expect to get much from him.

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:20.510
He's the worst of the cases from the mainland.

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:22.010
And Chise?

00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:24.680
We haven't found her yet.

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:28.750
We've got all available personnel looking for her.

00:13:29.090 --> 00:13:31.620
But the rumor among the troops is...

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:34.920
anyone who sees her, dies.

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:41.330
Commander Ito, sir! Someone to see you!

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:43.070
I'm coming in!

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:46.640
It wasn't my fault...

00:13:46.710 --> 00:13:50.040
Commander Ito, Mr. Kawahara from the lab is here...

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:52.540
to ask you about Chise.

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:55.050
It's been a while...

00:13:55.190 --> 00:13:57.950
Medicine, maintenance, it's no good!

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:01.890
She's no longer human!

00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:06.130
I didn't want to see...

00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:11.000
I didn't want to know!

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:23.600
Shuji, where'd you go?

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:25.510
Come join us.

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:27.840
Sorry, gotta go to the classroom.

00:14:28.420 --> 00:14:29.330
The classroom?

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:32.950
I need to talk to your sister.

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:38.560
Do you mind if we come too?

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:39.560
No.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.090
Iku, let's go.

00:14:41.300 --> 00:14:42.290
You better not.

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:45.110
Why? Is it OK, Shuji?

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:51.530
Are you envious, Atsushi? I've gotten pretty popular.

00:14:57.680 --> 00:14:59.800
It just... couldn't be helped.

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:03.780
This is all that's left.

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:07.120
What's this medicine for?

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:09.780
It couldn't be helped.

00:15:10.390 --> 00:15:14.850
We all live by technology or die by it.

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:17.230
It's one or the other.

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:22.630
It couldn't be helped.

00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:25.260
Shuji, I'm almost there.

00:15:26.010 --> 00:15:26.720
Wait for me.

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:34.110
She's made of the same elements that make up any human being.

00:15:36.520 --> 00:15:39.350
No one can save her from her fate.

00:15:43.690 --> 00:15:45.350
Is Chise here?

00:15:46.560 --> 00:15:49.030
I thought she might be with you.

00:15:50.530 --> 00:15:54.800
You knew the truth, yet you closed your eyes to it.

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:58.170
That, too, couldn't be helped.

00:15:59.010 --> 00:16:00.660
It's no one's fault.

00:16:01.740 --> 00:16:02.970
It can be helped!

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:05.640
It's got to be!

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:11.620
Damn!

00:16:13.770 --> 00:16:14.690
Damn it!

00:16:29.310 --> 00:16:32.370
Atsushi, this is what I get...

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:37.070
for hurting people, for not protecting anyone...

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:40.580
for being useless.

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:44.480
Akemi, I'm sorry, sorry.

00:16:48.220 --> 00:16:51.750
My husband... he's dead.

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:02.870
How many days will these last?

00:17:10.280 --> 00:17:11.840
<i>Wait for me, Shuji.</i>

00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:16.050
<i>I'll be there soon. I can walk in a bit.</i>

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:22.680
Please, Shuji. Make love to me.

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:31.600
Please do it.

00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:38.030
Ms. Fuyumi, I can't.

00:17:43.900 --> 00:17:49.250
I'm sorry, Shuji. I'm scared.

00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:52.280
You once told me,

00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:58.070
that you'd protect me in his place.

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:03.700
You promised, remember?

00:18:18.710 --> 00:18:20.090
<i>Stupid pervert!</i>

00:18:23.720 --> 00:18:27.680
<i>What kind of way is that</i> <i>to talk, Akemi?</i>

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:30.350
<i>With tears and all...</i>

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:35.090
<i>I'm just a dumb kid.</i>

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:42.260
No, Shuji, not like that!

00:18:42.340 --> 00:18:44.110
That doesn't help.

00:18:44.300 --> 00:18:45.830
Be gentle!

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:47.200
Let me go!

00:18:59.020 --> 00:19:00.110
Shuji...

00:19:01.220 --> 00:19:02.920
not like this.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:06.220
This is what you taught me.

00:19:07.030 --> 00:19:07.890
Shuji...

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:10.290
Fuyumi, I'm weak.

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:12.860
I can't protect you.

00:19:16.910 --> 00:19:21.310
I can barely take care of myself.

00:19:21.710 --> 00:19:23.230
I'm just a kid.

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:29.770
But if I could protect a girl instead of myself...

00:19:30.450 --> 00:19:34.290
there's only one.

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:37.750
And you're not her.

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:44.160
I know. When I looked at you and saw my husband,

00:19:44.770 --> 00:19:48.640
and you touched me, it felt so good I couldn't help myself.

00:19:50.240 --> 00:19:53.830
You knew that, but still you came to me.

00:19:55.140 --> 00:19:59.100
I see now that you're old enough to be cruel.

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:06.640
You were so simple-minded, but I liked it anyway.

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:21.290
It's a shame you had to grow up.

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:29.300
<i>I'd never been aggressive</i> <i>with Fuyumi before that.</i>

00:20:30.070 --> 00:20:33.440
<i>Now I realized,</i>

00:20:34.280 --> 00:20:38.850
<i>that my love for her had been</i> <i>just a school boy fantasy.</i>

00:20:41.790 --> 00:20:43.620
<i>Ms. Fuyumi, I'm sorry.</i>

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:46.490
<i>I had wanted to kiss you...</i>

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:48.900
<i>and fool around with you.</i>

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:54.630
<i>To do things I'd be afraid</i> <i>to do with my girlfriend.</i>

00:20:56.170 --> 00:20:58.500
<i>I was just pretending</i> <i>I'd protect you.</i>

00:21:00.140 --> 00:21:03.240
<i>I didn't want to see my true self.</i>

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:07.180
<i>Ms. Fuyumi, I'm sorry.</i>

00:21:12.590 --> 00:21:16.960
<i>I never saw Ms. Fuyumi again.</i>

00:21:35.710 --> 00:21:37.270
I'm back, Shuji.

00:21:40.150 --> 00:21:41.710
You know, I...

00:21:43.420 --> 00:21:44.980
Dummy, what kept you?

00:22:06.140 --> 00:22:09.340
So much has happened.

00:22:10.110 --> 00:22:12.170
Yeah, same here.

00:22:13.950 --> 00:22:14.680
Shall we go?

00:22:15.420 --> 00:22:16.010
Yeah.

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:43.420
A rift opened up upon my heart

00:22:43.790 --> 00:22:49.990
And I went through the night sleepless, sighing constantly

00:22:50.670 --> 00:22:59.340
Before I realize, it's turned to morning

00:23:02.280 --> 00:23:08.660
I want to hear your voice

00:23:09.180 --> 00:23:13.250
I want to feel your warmth

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:19.460
Thoughts of you well up within me

00:23:20.640 --> 00:23:25.310
And my tears begin to overflow

00:23:25.320 --> 00:23:36.570
Goodbye my beloved, I am still unable to forget about you

00:23:36.730 --> 00:23:46.740
Having all of this end with just a single word of goodbye

00:23:47.240 --> 00:23:51.570
Fills me with sorrow

00:24:00.390 --> 00:24:03.880
Chise, you got a job in a noodle shop? Can you handle it?

00:24:04.260 --> 00:24:06.490
A new town, a new life...

00:24:06.660 --> 00:24:09.390
